{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9f96a334a4ce6f6b05b4c9a95746297fd4a222a2dbaa53a29282cabccbdb6599","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar.mcp_server.build_server()","key_entities":["mcp.server.fastmcp.server.Settings","FastMCP","IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning","Settings.model_rebuild()","rebar.mcp_server.build_server()","DefaultSettingsSource","pydantic_settings.sources.utils"],"problem_keywords":["pydantic-settings","forward-reference","lazy import","MCP v1","incomplete field definition","warning suppression","lifespan annotation"],"propositions":["MCP v1 defines generic Settings before FastMCP under postponed annotations, leaving Settings.model_fields[\"lifespan\"] unresolved as a ForwardRef with _complete=False","On first FastMCP construction, pydantic-settings 2.15 inspects the incomplete FieldInfo and emits IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning, causing build_server() to abort when the warning is promoted to an error","Calling Settings.model_rebuild() after lazy import resolves the forward reference and eliminates the warning on first construction without changing runtime behavior or schema","The fix must invoke Settings.model_rebuild() at build_server's lazy MCP import boundary before either HTTP or stdio transport construction completes"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787806855340701001,"uuid":"5b68dc93-4b15-41dd-8729-cc5bb5b0c86f"}